  THE CONFOUND AND THE SECONDARY. `label` runs the SAME estimator on the
  object sequence itself: the draw is an i.i.d. coin, so it must read ~0 and a
  non-zero reading would mean clustered errors were inherited rather than the
  index's. `probe` is the read-back window, scored against its own assignment.
    arm       label primary +- SE    probe primary +- SE   (NEITHER is read by a verdict)
    DERIVED      +0.0102 +- 0.0068 (n=24)   -0.2780 +- 0.0231 (n=24)
    PINNED       +0.0000 +- 0.0000 (n= 0)   +0.0000 +- 0.0000 (n= 0)
    IID171       +0.0026 +- 0.0095 (n=12)   +0.0000 +- 0.0000 (n= 0)
    BLK8         +0.0026 +- 0.0095 (n=12)   +0.0000 +- 0.0000 (n= 0)

  THE HALF-SESSION ASSIGNMENT -- ADDED AFTER THE SMOKE AND SAID SO. The 150k
  smoke found 20 of 24 DERIVED creatures with a DEGENERATE assignment, where
  §53 reports `degenerate 0` on 36 of 36 at 450k: the index starts COLLAPSED
  and splits as the conscience separates the prototypes, so the assignment is
  not stationary. This scores each half with the same `modal` lambda and asks
  whether the halves AGREE. It is the question §55 named, it is a SECONDARY,
  and no verdict below reads it -- the pre-registered primary is untouched.
    arm       agree  FLIPPED  a half degenerate   (of the non-degenerate creatures)
    DERIVED      21        1                  2   24
    PINNED       12        0                  0   12
    IID171       12        0                  0   12
    BLK8         12        0                  0   12

  CLAUSE 0 (FIRST) -- LIVENESS AND IDENTIFICATION. An arm with no scored
  window, or an index the genome could not run, is VOID. The primary is
  UNDEFINED at m < 2, so the identification check asks how many DERIVED
  creatures carry m >= 5 -- asserting identification is how a gate that cannot
  fail gets written (`vacuity-gate-cannot-guard-a-rejection`).
    DERIVED  ok    creatures 24/24  windows 4944  ctx_slots 2  present 1.0000
    PINNED   ok    creatures 12/12  windows 2472  ctx_slots 2  present 1.0000
    IID171   ok    creatures 12/12  windows 2472  ctx_slots 2  present 1.0000
    BLK8     ok    creatures 12/12  windows 2472  ctx_slots 2  present 1.0000
    DERIVED  w_obs 0.2409 against §53's 0.1712 (|d| 0.0697, tol 0.03)  *** FAIL
    DERIVED  m >= 5 on 24 of 24 creatures (need 20), degenerate 0  PASS

  CLAUSE 1 -- THE EXACT SELF-TEST. On PINNED the pin IS the label, so no
  window can be mis-assigned: m must be ZERO, not small.
    PINNED   m 0 over 2472 windows, degenerate 0  PASS

  CLAUSE 2 -- THE CALIBRATION, BOTH ENDS OF THE ESTIMATOR'S RANGE. IID171 is
  §54's mode 3 (a coin per trial), so its primary is ZERO by construction and
  its across-creature SD is THE ERROR MODEL -- not the pre-flight arithmetic
  (`power-is-not-the-error-model`). BLK8 draws the same coin once per 8
  consecutive teaching windows, so every error has a neighbour and `obs` must
  read 1.0000 bar one block truncated by the session's end.
    IID171   primary +0.0149 +- 0.0238 (tol +0.0567)   w_obs 0.1610   PASS
    BLK8     obs 1.0000 (need >= 0.98), primary +0.7131 (need >= +0.60), w_obs 0.1667   PASS
    the knob rates 0.1610 and 0.1667 against 0.1712, tolerances DERIVED per arm from
             its own effective draw count (B = 1 and 8): 0.0227 and 0.0643  PASS
    DERIVED  |exact - shuffle| 0.0095 (tol 0.02)  PASS
    IID171   |exact - shuffle| 0.0075 (tol 0.02)  PASS
    BLK8     |exact - shuffle| 0.0097 (tol 0.02)  PASS
    the formula  checked on 3 of 4 arms (ZERO would be a gate that cannot
                 fail, so zero is a FAILURE and not a pass)  PASS
    THE ERROR MODEL. Pre-flight said SE 0.0158 at 450k on 24 creatures and
    0.0112 at 900k. IID171's realised SE is 0.0238 on 12 creatures, per-creature
    SD 0.0826.

  CLAUSE 3 -- THE VERDICT, on DERIVED's TEACHING windows. Pre-registered three
  ways in ROADMAP §56 before any number existed. The boundary +0.0567 is 2/m at
  450k's window count and is FROZEN across budgets; realised m is 49.6, which
  would give +0.0403, printed for disclosure and NOT used.
    across creatures  primary +0.2011 +- 0.0280 (n = 24), 95% CI [+0.1463, +0.2559]
    obs 0.6125 against an exact null of 0.4114; longest error run 5.3 windows

    *** NO VERDICT BY REGISTRATION, not verdict C: 450000 ticks against the
    verdict budget of 900000. Every column above is a comparability reading
    against §53 and §55 and the gates below still say whether the instrument
    held. Nothing here is a verdict on the arrangement.
    the gates at this budget: AT LEAST ONE FAILED -- see clauses 0-2 above

    AND WHAT §56 CANNOT SETTLE, SAID IN THE PRE-REGISTRATION. `blocked`
    detects clustering at any scale >= 2 windows. The clamp-walk mechanism
    needs runs long enough to walk `bias_ctx_` to the opposite clamp, and the
    archive does not contain that length -- `retention` erased with a
    conflicting PHASE of thousands of trials, which bounds nothing at the scale
    of tens. No threshold on the 8+ bucket is pre-registered, because inventing
    one here is how a verdict gets fitted to data.
